    "result_text": "The implementation is already complete and the full suite is green. Let me summarize what I verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change \u2014 **all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`** \u2014 is fully implemented in the codebase, and the entire test suite passes (**255 tests, BUILD SUCCESS**), including the new acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson`.\n\n### What I verified\n\n**Central builder** \u2014 `rest/escalation/ProblemDetails.java` produces a Spring `ProblemDetail` with all four required members (`type` = `about:blank`, `title` = exception simple name, `status` from `HttpStatus`, `detail`), plus extra `timestamp`/`schemaValidationErrors` properties.\n\n**Every in-scope rejection handler routes through it and sends `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>`:**\n- **400**: `ValidationExceptionHandler` (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`), `FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`, `InvalidAddress/Email/Postcode/TelephoneExceptionHandler`\n- **409**: `DuplicateOwnerIdentityExceptionHandler`, `OwnerCityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`\n- **429**: `OwnerDailyLimitExceptionHandler`\n\n**Wiring is intact** \u2014 each handler is bound to its exception via `src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/*.yml`, and the app boots and registers all endpoints cleanly.\n\n**No bypass paths** \u2014 there are no leftover Spring `@RestController`/`@RestControllerAdvice`/`@ExceptionHandler` classes; every rejection flows through the OfficeFloor escalation handlers above. Handlers outside the 400/409/429 scope are unaffected (404 \u2192 empty body, idempotent replay \u2192 200).\n\n**Content type confirmed on the wire** \u2014 the acceptance test asserts `content type application/problem+json` and `$.status == 400` for a missing-`city` create, and it passes. The 409/429 handlers use the identical `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` send pattern, so serialization yields the same media type.\n\nThe test suite was run offline (`./mvnw -o test`) and is green, so no further changes were needed.",
